    "id": "lem:exact-coverage-repair",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(0\\le\\rho<1\\), and let \\(\\widetilde K\\) be a randomized rule satisfying\n\\[\n \\inf_{v\\in V}\\inf_{h\\in D_v}P_h\\{v\\in\\widetilde K(W)\\}\n \\ge1-\\eta-\\rho.\n\\]\nSet \\(q=\\rho/(\\eta+\\rho)\\), and let \\(K^+=\\operatorname{Repair}_{\\eta,\\rho}(\\widetilde K)\\).  Then \\(K^+\\in\\mathcal C_\\eta\\), and\n\\[\n \\sup_{h\\in H_r}E_h\\ell\\{K^+(W)\\}\n \\le\n \\sup_{h\\in H_r}E_h\\ell\\{\\widetilde K(W)\\}\n +\\frac{D\\rho}{\\eta+\\rho}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Repair",
      "eta",
      "V",
      "Dv",
      "W",
      "Ceta",
      "Hr",
      "ell",
      "Dmax",
      "r"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:exact-repair",
      "def:minimax-profile"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Because \\(\\eta>0\\) and \\(\\rho\\ge0\\), the mixing probability \\(q=\\rho/(\\eta+\\rho)\\) lies in \\([0,1)\\).  For every \\(v\\in V\\) and \\(h\\in D_v\\), reporting \\(V\\) always covers \\(v\\).  Therefore\n\\[\n \\begin{aligned}\n P_h\\{v\\in K^+(W)\\}\n &\\ge q+(1-q)(1-\\eta-\\rho)\\\\\n &=\\frac{\\rho+\\eta(1-\\eta-\\rho)}{\\eta+\\rho}\n =1-\\eta.\n \\end{aligned} \\tag{12}\n\\]\nTaking the two infima in (12) proves \\(K^+\\in\\mathcal C_\\eta\\).  Since \\(0\\le\\ell(A)\\le D\\) for every action and \\(\\ell(V)=D\\), for every \\(h\\in H_r\\),\n\\[\n \\begin{aligned}\n E_h\\ell\\{K^+(W)\\}\n &=(1-q)E_h\\ell\\{\\widetilde K(W)\\}+qD\\\\\n &\\le E_h\\ell\\{\\widetilde K(W)\\}+qD.\n \\end{aligned} \\tag{13}\n\\]\nTaking the supremum in (13) and substituting \\(q\\) proves the risk inequality.",
